Grammar

Rule 0     S' -> loop_statement
Rule 1     loop_statement -> while_loop
Rule 2     loop_statement -> for_loop
Rule 3     while_loop -> WHILE condition COLON suite
Rule 4     for_loop -> FOR ID IN RANGE LPAREN NUMBER RPAREN COLON suite
Rule 5     suite -> NEWLINE INDENT statements DEDENT
Rule 6     statements -> statement
Rule 7     statements -> statements statement
Rule 8     statement -> PRINT STRING NEWLINE
Rule 9     statement -> ID PLUSEQUALS NUMBER NEWLINE
Rule 10    condition -> ID GT NUMBER
Rule 11    condition -> ID LT NUMBER
Rule 12    condition -> ID GE NUMBER
Rule 13    condition -> ID LE NUMBER
Rule 14    condition -> ID EQ NUMBER
Rule 15    condition -> ID NE NUMBER

Terminals, with rules where they appear

COLON                : 3 4
DEDENT               : 5
EQ                   : 14
FOR                  : 4
GE                   : 12
GT                   : 10
ID                   : 4 9 10 11 12 13 14 15
IN                   : 4
INDENT               : 5
LE                   : 13
LPAREN               : 4
LT                   : 11
NE                   : 15
NEWLINE              : 5 8 9
NUMBER               : 4 9 10 11 12 13 14 15
PLUSEQUALS           : 9
PRINT                : 8
RANGE                : 4
RPAREN               : 4
STRING               : 8
WHILE                : 3
error                :

Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

condition            : 3
for_loop             : 2
loop_statement       : 0
statement            : 6 7
statements           : 5 7
suite                : 3 4
while_loop           : 1

Parsing method: LALR

